---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Two ways an auction goes wrong" hint="Part one: several bidders hit the same auction at the same instant. Part two: a bidder who sniped in the last second. Change the design and watch who wins.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>With <b>6 bidders at once</b>, <b>blind write</b> overwrites the highest bid of the round in <b>154 of 200 rounds</b>, and the price goes down 464 times. <b>Version check without retry</b> keeps the price rising but rejects 1,000 valid bids, and still loses the top bid in 150 rounds. <b>Version check with retry</b> loses none. Set the slider to 1 and all three look correct.</li>
    <li>Leave the extension window at <b>none</b>: the sniper bids in the last second, the other bidder needs 45 seconds to react, and the item sells for <b>105</b> to a bidder who valued it at 220, while the bidder who valued it at 300 never gets to answer.</li>
    <li>Choose a window of <b>60 or 120 seconds</b>: each late bid restarts the clock, the bidders keep answering, and the auction ends when the sniper runs out of money, at <b>220</b>. A <b>30 second</b> window is shorter than the 45 second reaction time and changes nothing.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg aub" data-aub>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Bidders hitting one auction at the same instant <input type="range" min="1" max="10" value="6" data-c /> <b data-cval></b></label>
      <label>Extension window after a late bid <select class="pg-in" data-w>
        <option value="0" selected>none</option>
        <option value="30">30 seconds</option>
        <option value="60">60 seconds</option>
        <option value="120">120 seconds</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Bidder reaction time (seconds) <input type="range" min="5" max="90" value="45" data-r /> <b data-rval></b></label>
      <label>Limit on extensions <select class="pg-in" data-cap>
        <option value="0" selected>no limit</option>
        <option value="8">at most 8</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <h3>Concurrent bids, 200 rounds</h3>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Blind write</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Version check, no retry</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Version check, then retry</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
    </div>
    <h3>A last-second snipe</h3>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Who wins</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>Bids and extensions</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b6><h3>Did the higher-value bidder win?</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o6></span><span class="pg-note" data-n6></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: part one runs 200 rounds. In each round all bidders read the same price and each bids that price plus 5 to 40 (a seeded random multiple of 5). A bid applies in arrival order. Blind write stores whatever arrives last. The version check lets only the first writer of a round succeed, and the retry variant lets the others try once more against the new price, so a bid is rejected only if it is no longer above the price plus 5. A round "loses the top bid" if the price at its end is below the highest bid made in it. Part two: the price is 100 and Alice leads. Bob values the item at 220 and Alice at 300. Bob bids 105 one second before the end, then each bidder in turn answers with the price plus 5 after the reaction time, until the end passes or the next bid would exceed their own value. A bid made inside the window restarts the clock to the full window. A bid at or after the end is refused.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-aub]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const ROUNDS = 200; const STEP = 5;
    let seed = 2025; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const draws = Array.from({ length: ROUNDS * 10 }, () => 1 + Math.floor(rnd() * 8));
    type Race = { price: number; applied: number; rejected: number; wentDown: number; lostTop: number; retried: number };
    function race(mode: string, c: number): Race {
      let price = 100; let ver = 0; let wentDown = 0; let applied = 0; let rejected = 0; let lostTop = 0; let retried = 0;
      for (let r = 0; r < ROUNDS; r++) {
        const seenP = price; const seenV = ver; let top = 0;
        for (let i = 0; i < c; i++) {
          const bid = seenP + STEP * draws[r * 10 + i]; top = Math.max(top, bid);
          if (mode === 'blind') { if (bid < price) wentDown++; price = bid; applied++; }
          else if (ver === seenV) { price = bid; ver++; applied++; }
          else if (mode === 'retry') { if (bid >= price + STEP) { price = bid; ver++; applied++; retried++; } else rejected++; }
          else rejected++;
        }
        if (price < top) lostTop++;
      }
      return { price, applied, rejected, wentDown, lostTop, retried };
    }
    function snipe(win: number, react: number, cap: number) {
      let end = 1000; let t = 999; let price = 100; let leader = 'Alice'; let bids = 0; let ext = 0; let who = 'Bob';
      const value: Record<string, number> = { Alice: 300, Bob: 220 };
      while (t < end) {
        const amt = price + STEP; if (amt > value[who]) break;
        price = amt; leader = who; bids++;
        if (win > 0 && end - t < win && (cap === 0 || ext < cap)) { end = t + win; ext++; }
        who = who === 'Bob' ? 'Alice' : 'Bob'; t += react;
      }
      return { leader, price, bids, ext };
    }
    const setBox = (k: number, main: string, note: string, bad: boolean) => {
      q(`[data-o${k}]`).textContent = main; q(`[data-n${k}]`).textContent = note;
      q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${k}]`).style.setProperty('--c', bad ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
    };
    const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
    function draw() {
      const c = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-c]').value); const w = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-w]').value);
      const rt = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-r]').value); const cap = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cap]').value);
      q('[data-cval]').textContent = String(c); q('[data-rval]').textContent = String(rt);
      const a = race('blind', c); const b = race('nretry', c); const d = race('retry', c);
      setBox(1, `${a.lostTop} of ${ROUNDS} rounds lost the top bid`, `the price went down ${fmt(a.wentDown)} times`, a.lostTop > 0);
      setBox(2, `${b.lostTop} of ${ROUNDS} rounds lost the top bid`, `${fmt(b.rejected)} bids rejected as conflicts`, b.lostTop > 0);
      setBox(3, `${d.lostTop} of ${ROUNDS} rounds lost the top bid`, `${fmt(d.applied)} bids applied, ${fmt(d.retried)} of them after a retry`, d.lostTop > 0);
      const s = snipe(w, rt, cap); const fair = s.leader === 'Alice';
      setBox(4, `${s.leader} wins at ${s.price}`, fair ? 'Alice values the item at 300, Bob at 220' : 'Alice values the item at 300 but could not answer', !fair);
      setBox(5, `${s.bids} bids, ${s.ext} extensions`, w === 0 ? 'there is no window, so the end never moves' : (rt < w ? `a ${rt} second reaction fits inside a ${w} second window` : `a ${rt} second reaction does not fit inside a ${w} second window`), false);
      setBox(6, fair ? 'yes' : 'no', fair ? 'the item went to the bidder who wanted it most' : 'the sniper won because nobody had time to respond', !fair);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = c > 1 && (a.lostTop > 0 || b.lostTop > 0) || !fair; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const p1 = c === 1 ? 'With one bidder at a time all three write strategies look correct, which is why races are missed in testing.'
        : `With ${c} bidders at once, blind write lost the top bid in ${a.lostTop} rounds and the version check without retry in ${b.lostTop}, while the version check with retry lost none.`;
      const p2 = fair ? ` The extension window gave the other bidder time to answer, and the auction ended at ${s.price}, when the sniper ran out of money.`
        : ` ${w === 0 ? 'With no extension' : (rt < w ? `The limit of ${cap} extensions ran out, so the clock stopped moving and` : `A ${w} second window is not longer than the ${rt} second reaction time, so`)} the sniper won at ${s.price}${s.bids > 1 ? ` after ${s.bids} bids` : ''}.`;
      out.textContent = p1 + p2;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
